invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_word.h
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: p256_wide_mul_word drops the carry into the word above the four, so
  a product whose third high half and top low half carry loses 2^256 of
  its value. The inverse multiplies by factors below 2^32, whose products
  carry there about once in 2^33 calls, so the inverses' cases alone pass.
  bin/p256_equiv_test holds the word product to a reference on edge and
  random full words, whose products carry there in about half the cases.

--- old
    return high3 + carry;
--- new
    return high3;
